Cursor shape (DECSCUSR, `CSI Ps SP q`) support.

mosh has no dispatch entry for final byte `q` at all, so an application asking
for a cursor shape is silently ignored -- nvim's insert-mode bar cursor stays a
block over mosh.

This is upstream PR #1355 rebased onto decd9b7 (it does not apply cleanly: the
OSC 8 merge added `hyperlink` to the same DrawState::operator== line this
extends, so the two are combined here), plus a fix for a bug the upstream
maintainer identified and the author has not addressed:

  https://github.com/mobile-shell/mosh/pull/1355
  https://github.com/mobile-shell/mosh/issues/352 (open since 2012)

The bug: -1 is the "never set" sentinel, and Framebuffer::reset() (RIS, \033c)
puts cursor_shape back to it. Upstream's emit is guarded by `!= -1`, so after a
reset nothing is sent and the terminal keeps whatever shape was last requested
while our model believes it is default. Repro: printf '\033[6 q\033c'.
Emitting DECSCUSR 0 on the way back to -1 fixes it.

Style of the added code adjusted to match mosh's clang-format.

diff --git a/src/terminal/terminaldisplay.cc b/src/terminal/terminaldisplay.cc
index ca2ae86..3f0ead1 100644
--- a/src/terminal/terminaldisplay.cc
+++ b/src/terminal/terminaldisplay.cc
@@ -119,6 +119,16 @@ std::string Display::new_frame( bool initialized, const Framebuffer& last, const
     frame.append( tmp );
   }
 
+  if ( f.ds.cursor_shape != frame.last_frame.ds.cursor_shape ) {
+    /* -1 means "never set", which is also where RIS (\033c) puts us. Upstream
+       PR #1355 skips emitting in that case, so after a reset the terminal keeps
+       whatever shape was last requested while our model believes it is default
+       -- the two ends stay diverged until something else changes the shape.
+       Emitting DECSCUSR 0 (default) on the way back to -1 fixes that. */
+    snprintf( tmp, sizeof( tmp ), "\033[%d q", f.ds.cursor_shape < 0 ? 0 : f.ds.cursor_shape );
+    frame.append( tmp );
+  }
+
   /* has size changed? */
   if ( ( !initialized ) || ( f.ds.get_width() != frame.last_frame.ds.get_width() )
        || ( f.ds.get_height() != frame.last_frame.ds.get_height() ) ) {
